  "id": "theweave",
  "note": "The building is called The Weave and it was two stacked boxes. It is four long slabs now, each rotated against the one below and crossing it — a stack you cannot read the corners of, which is the whole of what the name is asking for. ⚠ A ROTATED SLAB CARRIES NOTHING: `anchored` takes its wall planes from UNYAWED boxes, so every part authored here is on the podium and nothing is hung above z 0.11. The slabs are still BOXES though, so they keep their wall texture and their lit windows — which is why this reads as a woven tower after dark rather than as a dark sculpture. See thespire.json for what happens when the same shape is attempted with drums. RENDER_TUNE.legacyArms puts the asc_weave arm back.",
